  "note": "Private test build for Mario Kart World on the S2Arm engine: patches 0332 to 0340 (0338 and 0341 withdrawn after review) on the verified 829 (docs/evidence/s2arm-mkw-60-0332-0341.md). The diagnosis of the 30 fps ceiling (translation on the game's thread, power cap, CPU/GPU serialisation) led to: the Fair thermal scale, the thermal guest QoS, the memory tier raised by compressed memory, the per-piece wait for the encode thread, the thermal DRS steps and the dark-frame probe off by default; the acquire sync published at the present that took the texture off screen, as on the device; the translation core built with -O2. Every patch has its S2A_RB_* switch. Nothing is measured on an iPhone yet. Also in, as pushed by the other sessions: the MeloNX Core 7cf4ff80 (pin 97dfda63, run 45303538300, artifact 14879952963: Hogwarts Legacy's blocking link check demands its warm-up), the libretro collection LibretroCores-67ce2d3b (DeSmuME 3D supersampling, [rb-perf] timings, 64 MiB JIT arena; Azahar and both Beetle PSX cores as in 829) with the libretro bridge's JIT reasons and RGB565 frames.",
